{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink bundle felt like the strongest next choice because I have used both Blink and Foscam cameras, and adding doorbell and indoor coverage gives me a concrete reason to consider it.",
    "The router, outlet extender, and Echo Studio bundle connect to my home viewing and connected-device interests, although that connection alone does not give me a reason to buy them today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The iPad Mini protector requires a device I have not indicated owning, and the internal SSD assumes a computer upgrade need that my monitor purchase does not establish.",
    "Buying a portable camcorder does not mean I want a desktop microphone or studio lighting stands; those serve recording activities I have not shown interest in.",
    "Earbuds and in-car Alexa do not address the home viewing and security needs reflected in my recent purchases."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into an interest in unrelated accessories, even when there is no clear use for them in my setup.",
    "My Fire TV and camcorder purchases seem to have been taken as reasons to suggest Alexa in the car and studio recording equipment, despite those being different uses."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated camera purchases make home monitoring a stronger connection than simply sharing a technology brand or feature.",
    "I need a clear added benefit before choosing another device: the Blink bundle could extend coverage, but its overlap with my existing camera still matters.",
    "Supporting accessories such as a router or outlet extender become relevant purchases when I have a connection or outlet problem; owning connected devices does not establish that need."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognized my home electronics interests but often missed the specific home viewing and security uses that would make another purchase worthwhile."
}"}
